course: dictionary
lesson: 2257
title: One word, two jobs
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Crayon can be a noun or a verb. A noun is a thing: a crayon is a stick of coloured wax for drawing and colouring. A verb is an action: to crayon is to draw or colour with crayons. The context tells you which one you are reading.
explain: «Wax crayons are made of melted coloured wax poured into moulds, cooled, checked and wrapped in paper labels by machine.» Here crayons are things made in a factory, so crayon is a noun. Ask yourself: is the word naming a thing, or telling me what someone does?
explain: Watch out for words that look like English but mean something else. In French, «un crayon» is a pencil, not a wax crayon, and «une trousse» is a pencil case, not trousers. Words from other languages can trick you, so check the sentence around them before you decide.
fact: A crayon is a stick of coloured wax for drawing and colouring.
fact: Crayon is a noun (a crayon, two crayons) and a verb (to crayon, she crayoned).
fact: «Wax crayons» are made of melted coloured wax, poured into moulds and then cooled.
fact: In French, «un crayon» means a pencil, and «une trousse» means a pencil case.
fact: In Chinese, «sè» means colour, so «hóngsè» means red colour.
exercise: «Wax crayons are made of melted coloured wax poured into moulds.» What are wax crayons made of? | Wood and lead | Paper and glue | *Melted coloured wax | Chewing gum
exercise: Ella's French book says «un crayon». In English, what does it mean? | A pencil case | A rubber | A wax crayon | *A pencil
exercise: «Step two: 40 - 12 = 28 crayons left.» If there were 40 crayons and 12 were lost, how many are left? | 52 | 40 | *28 | 12
test: «Lucy crayoned a picture of the sea.» What does crayoned mean here? | Cut out | Wrote a letter | Ate a snack | *Drew or coloured with crayons
test: «Une trousse» is a French word. What does it mean in English? | Trousers | *A pencil case | A sharpener | A rubber
exam: Ming says «hóngsè» and «lánsè» end in «sè». What does sè mean? | Crayon | Red | *Colour | Light
